[{:db/id 17592186138401 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f30dc369-9201-5339-acfb-6423eb9240e9" "question-55110545-b3e1-5cf7-8175-0d77be4e9f01" "question-8483f85d-e913-5b06-97f5-b1636ab469ac" "question-a905ef12-b46f-573f-8f59-c83381d8de89" "question-bcd116c0-6c77-5a3a-aa4a-fdb222617782"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138135 :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate $4^2.$\n\nTo evaluate $4^2,$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4}^{2}={{4\\times 4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{[math]2[/math] times}}=16\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138402 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-67f4609a-bf5e-5370-a6dc-848f8c2f3fef" "question-ca59627a-61c0-5ddb-824a-6032d58fc249" "question-ef349707-5a77-5407-8660-293dceb041c2" "question-3b68262c-4f64-5130-a6e1-d1cb3e865a03" "question-fdc760ae-ab2b-5525-82f1-1022c98537aa"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138136 :question/problem "What is the value of $5$ raised to the power of $3?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $5$ raised to the power of $3$ means $5^3.$\n\nTo compute this power, we start by writing it out with multiplication signs:\n![](images/e7/e7beecad2379c3be9452eb111496ed8c65a5d4f747874658167169bba6ff11c9.svg)\n\nNow, we compute the product. Since $5 \\times 5 = 25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{5\\times 5}_{⏟}}_{25}\\times 5 & =25\\times 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we work out ${\\color{blue}25} \\times 5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned} &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,{}_{2}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5^3=125.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138403 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-773cb4cb-362b-5414-b8bb-5906a1086fc1" "question-3f183567-7c74-5fbf-89e1-23612bbcb99c" "question-1b33d924-7eab-577d-ae85-a2f9c5ebfc75" "question-49d63c61-4b5e-531a-8049-3028c80de021" "question-90374c13-9ebe-5b30-938a-ec930bff9f54"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138137 :question/problem "Find the value of $6^1.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, ${\\color{blue}6}^{\\color{red}1}$ is in exponent form. The base is $\\color{blue}6$ and the exponent is ${\\color{red}1}.$ \n\nThis means that $\\color{blue}6$ is taken as a factor only once. Therefore,\n\n$$\n6^1 = 6.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138404 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-055bced7-1256-505d-bf41-0147f8e143ed" "question-c82d42be-b446-5866-87ca-88ea9428fb90" "question-ea112c87-3b39-503f-b604-c75805eee0b7" "question-47a275b6-8ed5-5b82-b1e3-8feb36ab37f8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186138138 :question/problem "Calculate the value of $0^5.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, ${\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{red}5}$ is in exponent form. The base is $\\color{blue}0$ and the exponent is ${\\color{red}5}.$ \n\nThis means that ${\\color{blue}0}$ is taken as a factor ${\\color{red}5}$ times. Therefore,\n![](images/ac/acfc8529f86ae7a3d9082c541da994c0c69ffccf33d01226593ae61cfb4d263a.svg)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f30dc369-9201-5339-acfb-6423eb9240e9" :question/id #uuid "f30dc369-9201-5339-acfb-6423eb9240e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-224033" :question/problem "What is the value of $9$ raised to the second power?\n\n$9$ raised to the second power is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate ${9}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${9}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{9}^{2}={{9\\times 9}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=81\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b805c8d7-74a6-5522-a93f-640553aa32c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b805c8d7-74a6-5522-a93f-640553aa32c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b805c8d7-74a6-5522-a93f-640553aa32c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-c5791977-ff66-58e7-87e1-c6140417cf63" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c5791977-ff66-58e7-87e1-c6140417cf63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c5791977-ff66-58e7-87e1-c6140417cf63" :answer/id #uuid "c5791977-ff66-58e7-87e1-c6140417cf63" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "81" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-55110545-b3e1-5cf7-8175-0d77be4e9f01" :question/id #uuid "55110545-b3e1-5cf7-8175-0d77be4e9f01" :question/math-academy-id "q-224152" :question/problem "What is the square of $3?$\n\nThe square of $3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "The square of $3$ is the same as ${3}^{2}.$\n\nTo evaluate ${3}^{2},$ we write it out with multiplication signs and then compute the product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{2}={{3\\times 3}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ times}}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f4bc28e-f642-5ec2-b8a8-5fe052b6282e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f4bc28e-f642-5ec2-b8a8-5fe052b6282e" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f4bc28e-f642-5ec2-b8a8-5fe052b6282e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ca49e0b4-682d-513d-b481-352b0f1e7624" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ca49e0b4-682d-513d-b481-352b0f1e7624"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ca49e0b4-682d-513d-b481-352b0f1e7624" :answer/id #uuid "ca49e0b4-682d-513d-b481-352b0f1e7624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8483f85d-e913-5b06-97f5-b1636ab469ac" :question/id #uuid "8483f85d-e913-5b06-97f5-b1636ab469ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-224147" :question/problem "What is the square of $5?$" :question/